.TH CYAML_DELETE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cyaml_delete \- remove and free the DOM node at a dot-separated path
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

ccol_retval_t cyaml_delete(cyaml root, const char *path);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Walks to the parent of the node that the path addresses, removes that
child and frees its whole subtree.  The path has the same
dot-separated syntax as in cyaml_get and cyaml_set.

When the parent is a dictionary, the leaf component is the key to
remove.  When it is a list, the leaf component must be a '#N' token,
so "#0" removes the first element.

The path is split at its LAST unescaped dot, so "a.b.c" targets the
key "c" inside the node at "a.b".  A path with no dot has root as its
parent.

The escapes '\e.' and '\e\e' give a literal dot and a literal
backslash in a key name, as they do in cyaml_get and cyaml_set.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_retval_t, which is ccol_success on success.
ccol_invalid_args for a NULL root, a NULL path, an empty path, a
malformed component and a path whose shape cannot apply to the tree.
A component is malformed when it is empty (nothing between two dots,
a leading dot, or a trailing dot), when it has bad '#N' index syntax
on a list, or when it is not well-formed UTF-8.  A shape cannot
apply when a component on a list is not '#N', or when the macro finds
any component under a scalar.  This code can come from any position
in the path, not only the leaf, and it wins over an absent component
earlier in the path.
ccol_key_not_found only when a well-formed component (a dictionary
key or a '#N' index) is absent, at any position, and when a list
index with correct syntax is out of range, however many digits it
has.
ccol_not_enough_memory when an internal allocation fails.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cyaml_delete(doc, "server.debug");
cyaml_delete(doc, "hosts.#0");
cyaml_delete(doc, "users.alice.address");
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_get (3),
.BR cyaml_set (3),
.BR cyaml_dictionary_remove (3),
.BR cyaml_list_remove (3)
